![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When a row is accepted via the `QuestionRenderModel` fallback (`fallbackAccepted` is true), it does not require a standard source visual receipt. However, the current implementation of `receiptRef` does not account for `fallbackAccepted` and will return a status of `'missing'` or `'missing_or_not_accepted'` if `productionInfo` or `receiptInfo` is not accepted or missing. This will cause the validator check `visual_rows_blocked_or_fully_gated` to fail because it strictly expects `status === 'accepted'` for final eligible rows. Passing `fallbackAccepted` to `receiptRef` and returning `status: 'accepted'` when it is true resolves this issue.

```javascript
function receiptRef(receiptInfo, paths, required, productionInfo = null, fallbackAccepted = false) {
  if (fallbackAccepted) {
    return {
      required: false,
      status: 'accepted',
    };
  }
  if (!required) {
    return {
      required: false,
      status: 'not_required_for_text_only_row',
    };
  }
  const producedReceiptRef = productionReceiptRef(productionInfo, paths);
  if (producedReceiptRef) return producedReceiptRef;
```

