When `fallbackAccepted` is true and `productionInfo` is null, the superseded blockers (such as `required_source_visual_not_accepted` or `source_visual_receipt_missing`) are not filtered out of the `blockers` array because the filter condition only checks `!productionInfo`. This leaves stale blockers on a fully accepted fallback row. Updating the filter to check for either `productionInfo` or `fallbackAccepted` ensures these blockers are correctly removed.

```suggestion
  ].filter((blocker) => (
    !(productionInfo || fallbackAccepted) || !SUPERSEDED_VISUAL_BLOCKER_IDS.has(blocker?.blocker_id)
  ));
```

